# Keep the Docker build context small and, more importantly, free of host build output:
# copying a host-built bin/ or obj/ into the image is the classic cause of "works on my
# machine" image drift, because the restore inside the image would be skipped.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/logs/

.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/TestResults/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/secrets.json
**/appsettings.*.local.json

docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
README.md
LICENSE
*.md
